            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case New York State Rifle & Pistol Association, Inc. v. City of New York challenges New York City\u2019s restrictive premises\u2011license requirement and its rule that firearm transport must be continuous and uninterrupted."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the regulations treat the Second Amendment as a home\u2011bound right and unlawfully prohibit transporting firearms, even when unloaded and locked, beyond the curtilage."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners contend that the city\u2019s restrictions are unconstitutional because they treat the Second Amendment as a home\u2011bound right and prohibit transporting firearms, even when unloaded and locked, beyond the curtilage."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that the ban causes economic harms by violating their constitutional rights."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2a517d3de29f-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 65,
                "start": 65
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners seek relief that would allow the full exercise of the right of defense of hearth and home, including the ability to transport firearms between lawful locations."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Wall",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Wall, petitioners cite Federal Rule 54(c) to argue that the prayer of relief should not be bound by a default judgment when the case has been litigated on the merits."
        }
      ],
